{% if team %}
## Agent Teams

Agent Teams are enabled (`CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS=1`, mode `{{ team_mode }}`).
For work that benefits from parallel exploration, spawn a team instead of delegating
sequentially: run `/team <task>`, or ask in natural language — e.g. "spawn 3 teammates to
review this from security, performance and test-coverage angles". Each teammate reuses one
of the agent roles above, runs in its own context, and coordinates through the shared task
list and direct messages.

- Give each teammate an independent slice; don't let two edit the same files.
- 3–5 teammates is the sweet spot; teams use more tokens than a single session.
- Experimental. `teammateMode` is set in this project's `settings.json`, but it's a
  user-level preference — move it to `~/.claude/settings.json` if it isn't honored here.
{% if plan_gate or risk_rounds or confidence_threshold or approval_gate %}
### Governed workflow

This team runs under governance gates. The team keeps its working state under `.claude/team/`:
`plan.md` (the shared task list, intent, and risk register) and `confidence/<task-id>.txt`
(a teammate's self-assessed confidence). These are created at runtime — don't pre-author them.
{% if plan_gate %}
- **Plan approval first.** Run `/team-plan` before executing: interview, draft the shared task
  list, present it, and take questions and requested improvements until the user approves. The
  `TaskCreated` hook blocks execution tasks until `.claude/team/plan.md` contains `Status: APPROVED`.
{%- endif %}
{% if confidence_threshold %}
- **Confidence gate.** Before completing a task, a teammate records its confidence in
  `.claude/team/confidence/<task-id>.txt`; the `TaskCompleted` hook blocks completion below
  ≥ {{ confidence_threshold }}%. A teammate may not pick up the next task until the current one clears the gate.
{%- endif %}
{% if risk_rounds %}
- **Risk mitigation rounds.** Every risk in the register gets its own mitigation round; leave it
  `Mitigation: pending` until addressed, then mark it `done` or `accepted`. The `TeammateIdle`
  hook keeps teammates working while any risk is still pending.
{%- endif %}
{% if approval_gate %}
- **Execution-approval gate (hard line).** No agent may perform a high-impact external action —
  `ssh`, cloud mutations (`aws`/`gcloud`/`az`), `git push`/`merge`, `gh pr merge`/`release`,
  `terraform apply`, `kubectl`/`helm`, deploys, or publishes — until a **human** reviews and
  unlocks execution. Unlock only from your own terminal (never through a tool call):
  `touch .claude/team/execution-approved`; delete it to re-lock. A deterministic `PreToolUse`
  hook enforces this and refuses any attempt by an agent to create the marker itself. Plan and
  local edits are allowed before the line; crossing it into external side effects is not.
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
{% endif %}